#Problem APEX 5.2.18-21

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Integrals)
## DBsection(Conceptual understanding of integration)
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## KEYWORDS(definite integral, integral properties)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('5.2')
## Problem1('18 21')
## Updated July 2023

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
Context('Numeric');

$a = non_zero_random(-15, 15);
$b = non_zero_random(-15, 15);
$c = non_zero_random(-15, 15);
$d = non_zero_random(-15, 15);

$ans1 = Compute($a + $c);
$cd   = Compute($c + $d);
$ans2 = Compute($b - $cd);
$ba   = Compute($b - $a);
$ans3 = Compute(3 * $ba + 2 * $d);
$ans4 = Compute(-$cd / $b);

BEGIN_PGML
Let
[```
\begin{aligned}
  \int_{0}^2 f(x) \, dx & = [$a],& \quad
  \int_{0}^3 f(x) \, dx & = [$b], \\
  \int_{0}^2 g(x) \, dx &= [$c],& \quad
  \int_{2}^3 g(x) \, dx &= [$d].
  \end{aligned}
```]

Use these values to evaluate the given definite integrals.

a) [`` \int_{0}^2 \left(f(x) + g(x)\right) \, dx = ``] [_]{$ans1}{20}

b) [`` \int_{0}^3 \left(f(x) - g(x)\right) \, dx = ``] [_]{$ans2}{20}

c) [``  \int_{2}^3 \left(3f(x) + 2g(x)\right) \, dx = ``] [_]{$ans3}{20}

d) Find the value [`a`] such that
[``` \int_{0}^3 
   \left(a f(x) + g(x)\right) \, dx = 0. ```]
    
    [`a = `] [_]{$ans4}{20}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) 
[```
  \begin{aligned}
  \int_0^2 \left(f(x) + g(x)\right) \, dx
  &=  \int_0^2 f(x) \, dx + \int_0^2 g(x) \, dx \\
  &= [$a] + [$c] \\
  &= [$ans1].
  \end{aligned}
```]

b) First find the integral of [`g`] from 0 to 3.
[```
  \begin{aligned}
  \int_0^3 g(x) \, dx &= \int_0^2 g(x) \, dx +
  \int_2^3 g(x) \, dx \\
  &= [$c] + [$d] \\
  &= [$cd].
  \end{aligned}
```]
Then
[```
  \begin{aligned}
  \int_0^3 \left(f(x) - g(x)\right) \, dx
  &=  \int_0^3 f(x) \, dx - \int_0^3 g(x) \, dx \\
  &= [$b] - [$cd] \\
  &= [$ans2].
  \end{aligned}
```]

c) First find the integral of [`f`] from 2 to 3.
[```
  \begin{array}{rcl}
    \displaystyle\int_0^3 f(x) \, dx &=& 
    \displaystyle\int_0^2 f(x) \, dx +
    \int_2^3 f(x) \, dx \\
    [$b] &=& [$a] + \displaystyle\int_2^3 f(x) \, dx \\
    \displaystyle\int_2^3 f(x) \, dx &=& [$ba]
  \end{array}
```]
Then
[```
  \begin{aligned}
  \int_{2}^3
   \left(3f(x) + 2g(x)\right) \, dx &=
  3\int_{2}^3     
   f(x)  \, dx + 2\int_{2}^3
   g(x) \, dx \\
  &= 3([$ba]) + 2([$d]) \\
  &= [$ans3].
  \end{aligned}
```]

d) Substitute known values for the integrals.
[```
  \begin{array}{rcl}
    \displaystyle \int_{0}^3 
   \left(a f(x) + g(x)\right) \, dx &=& 0 \\
   a \displaystyle \int_0^3 f(x) \, dx
   + \int_0^3 g(x) \, dx &=& 0\\
   a([$b]) + [$cd] &=& \\
   a &=& [$ans4]
  \end{array}
```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();

